    <Label Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="Measuring Across a Lake" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="57.5" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="How far is it from the tent to the cabin, when a lake is in the way and you can't walk straight across?\n\nCheck &quot;Help 1&quot; and &quot;Help 2&quot; for the trick, and &quot;Show&quot; for the answer. It uses congruent triangles — the same idea surveyors used before there were satellites.\n\nDrag the tent and the cabin." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="105.5" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
